note.text:
Needs are things we must have: food, soap, school books. Wants are nice to have, but we can live without them: sweets, a new phone. When money is short, buy the needs first: they are the priority.
A good shopping list:
• has a title, for example “Shopping list for Saturday”;
• has one item on each line, with the quantity and the price;
• puts the most important items first;
• adds up the prices, and the total is not more than the money you have.
Before you go to the market, check the list again: is anything missing? Can you buy everything with your money?
